This mirrors the licensing of Cloudflare's own developer tooling (wrangler is
`MIT OR Apache-2.0`; workerd is Apache-2.0), so shopcf composes cleanly with the
platform it runs on.

Why both: MIT is the most permissive and familiar option, while Apache-2.0 adds
an explicit patent grant (section 3) and patent-retaliation terms that MIT is
silent about. Downstream users pick whichever fits their legal posture.

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution intentionally submitted
for inclusion in this work shall be dual-licensed as above, without any
additional terms or conditions. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the contributor
licensing terms.
